# 🍋 Guava Home — Hardware & Setup Guide

This guide covers the critical hardware wiring, specific library dependencies, and repository setup required to successfully compile and run the Guava Home system.

## 📚 Library Dependencies

Guava Home relies on several excellent open-source libraries. You can install all of these via the **Library Manager** in the Arduino IDE (`Sketch` > `Include Library` > `Manage Libraries`).

* **DHT sensor library** by Adafruit
* **Adafruit Unified Sensor** by Adafruit (Required dependency for the DHT library)
* **LiquidCrystal_I2C** by Frank de Brabander
* **UniversalTelegramBot** by Brian Lough
* **MFRC522** by GithubCommunity

### ⚠️ Critical Warning: ArduinoJson Version
Guava Home is built using **ArduinoJson Version 6**. 
Do **NOT** install ArduinoJson Version 7.x, as the syntax was completely overhauled and it will cause catastrophic compilation failures. If you are using the Library Manager, select version `6.21.5` (or any 6.x version) from the dropdown menu before clicking Install.

